OL,1,Vk4                               G4/23
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGFRANCE OFFERS TO SEND
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGTROOPS TO GULF
OL,4,F
OL,5, France has offered to send troops to
OL,6, Saudi Arabia after Iraqi soldiers
OL,7, raided the French ambassador's
OL,8, residence in Kuwait.
OL,10,FPresident Mitterrand said 4,000
OL,11,Fsoldiers would be sent to Saudi Arabia
OL,12,Fprovided King Fahd agreed.
OL,14,FHe ordered the expulsion of Iraqi
OL,15,Fmilitary attaches, intelligence agents
OL,16,Fand Iraqis in France for training.
OL,18,FThe Iraqi ambassador to France has said
OL,19,FIraq "will take reciprocal measures
OL,20,Fat a diplomatic level" to what he said
OL,21,Fwas an "unjustified escalation".
OL,23,D]FFromG15-09-90F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789475634
OL,1,Vk4                               G5/23
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGFRANCE URGES UN SECURITY
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGCOUNCIL MEETING
OL,4,D
OL,5, France has called for an immediate
OL,6, United Nations Security Council meeting
OL,7, on Iraq's forced entry into the French
OL,8, and other embassies in Kuwait.
OL,10,FThe Council is expected to hold
OL,11,Finformal consultations this evening.
OL,13,FEarlier, France urged the UN to widen
OL,14,Fthe blockade of Iraq to air traffic and
OL,15,Fcalled for sanctions against states
OL,16,Fbreaking the UN embargo.
OL,18,FIn a meeting with the Italian prime
OL,19,Fminister, US Secretary of State James
OL,20,FBaker said he favoured sanctions
OL,21,Fagainst nations breaking the embargo.
OL,23,D]FFromG15-09-90F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789475634
OL,1,Vk4                               G6/23
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGWEST GERMANY TO GIVE
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pG#1BN TO GULF EFFORT
OL,4,D
OL,5, West Germany says it is going to give
OL,6, around #1 billion in financial and
OL,7, material aid to the Gulf operation.
OL,9,FThe aid will include contributions to
OL,10,Fthe United States and countries hit by
OL,11,Fthe UN sanctions against Iraq.
OL,13,FThe announcement came after a meeting
OL,14,Fbetween Chancellor Kohl and the US
OL,15,FSecretary of State James Baker.
OL,17,FWest Germany has been under intense
OL,18,Fpressure to do more to help in the
OL,19,FGulf, although its constitution forbids
OL,20,Fit from sending its military outside
OL,21,Fthe NATO area.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]FFromG15-09-90F  teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11807
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1789475634
OL,1,Vk4                               G7/23
OL,2,Vj5{5jj5~sGGULF FORCE COST "MAY RULE
OL,3,Vj5op0ozz5pGOUT TAX CUTS": PM
OL,4,D
OL,5, Mrs Thatcher has indicated the cost of
OL,6, sending British forces to the Gulf may
OL,7, reduce the likelihood of tax cuts
OL,8, before the next general election.
OL,10,FInterviewed in the Scotland on Sunday
OL,11,Fnewspaper, the Prime Minister said it
OL,12,Fcould delay the Government aim of
OL,13,Fcutting income tax to 20p in the pound.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FShe said cuts would depend on how long
OL,16,Fthe crisis lasted and whether United
OL,17,FNations sanctions succeeded.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FAsked if she would back US President
OL,20,FBush if he decided on a military
OL,21,Fstrike, she said: "I cannot tell".
OL,23,D]FFromG15-09-90F  teletextarchive.com
